# Requirements

Parameters: a1 is the constant level of c1, s3 the amplitude of the c3 sine, f its frequency in Hz.

### H1: Weaker c1 at 2 Hz stroking lands x in the goal window

WHEN c1 is held at a1 = -0.5 and c3 is a unit sine at f = 2 Hz with the other inputs 0, THE system SHALL reach x between 0.3 and 0.5 m with |heading| under 20 deg and |y| under 0.2 m.

```prediction
# relies on: R11, R9
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.3, 0.55]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a1 = -0.5
s3 = 1
f = 2

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "heading"
range = [-25, 20]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
a1 = -0.5
s3 = 1
f = 2
```

### H2: The given E9 point reproduces on this bench

WHEN c1 is held at -1 and c3 is a unit sine at f = 2 Hz with the other inputs 0, THE system SHALL reach x near 0.62 m with heading near 0 deg.

```prediction
# relies on: none
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.5, 0.75]
label = "inside"
[prediction.when]
a1 = -1
s3 = 1
f = 2

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "heading"
range = [-20, 20]
label = "inside"
[prediction.when]
a1 = -1
s3 = 1
f = 2
```

Notes: H1 showed x of about -0.05 for a1 = -0.5 and -0.75 at f = 2, so this checks whether the given beliefs apply at all.

### H3: A travelling wave across c0..c4 moves this body, with direction set by the sign of the phase lag

WHEN all five inputs are 1 Hz unit sines with phase lag ph = 1 rad per channel index, THE system SHALL reach |x| above 0.1 m, and the sign of x SHALL flip when ph = -1.

```prediction
# relies on: none
[[prediction]]
id = "P1"
measurement = "x"
range = [0.1, 1.5]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
amp = 1
f = 1
ph = 1

[[prediction]]
id = "P2"
measurement = "x"
range = [-1.5, -0.1]
label = "new-combination"
[prediction.when]
amp = 1
f = 1
ph = -1
```

Notes: H1 and H2 showed c1 constant plus c3 sine gives x of about -0.05 only. This is a first probe of the other channels.

### H4: Constant c1 at +1 moves the body in x on this bench

WHEN c1 is held at +1 with the other inputs 0, THE system SHALL end with |x| above 0.1 m, and WHEN all five inputs are held at +1 or all at -1, THE system SHALL end with |x| above 0.1 m.

```prediction
